---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../styles/global.css';
import OfficialSources from '../../components/OfficialSources.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, GA4_ID, LEGAL } from '../../data/site-config';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy policy for this debt payoff calculator 2026"
  description="Balances, APRs and monthly payments you enter stay in your browser. Google Analytics audience cookies, no ads, cookieless stability checks and your rights."
>
  <section class="pt-2 pb-16 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto prose prose-lg">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-text mb-8">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-muted mb-8">Last updated: October 17, 2026</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text mt-8 mb-4">The short version</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        MyDebtPayoff.com is published by {LEGAL.entityName}. It shows no ads and never sees the figures you
        type. Visits are counted with Google Analytics, which sets audience measurement cookies, and page
        stability is checked anonymously with Microsoft Clarity, which sets none.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text mt-8 mb-4">Your debt figures</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        The credit card balances, loan amounts, APRs, minimum payments and extra monthly payments you enter to
        compare the avalanche and snowball methods are computed by JavaScript in your own browser. They are never
        sent to a server, never stored in a database and not saved on your device either: close the tab and they
        are gone.
      </p>

      <h2 id="cookies" class="text-2xl font-bold text-text mt-8 mb-4">Cookies</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        What you type in the calculators is never stored in your browser. The only cookies are those of Google
        Analytics audience measurement, described below. There is no advertising, no ad network, no Facebook Pixel
        and no social media tracker.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Provider</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Lifetime</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>_ga</code></td><td>Google Analytics</td><td>Tell visitors apart with a random identifier</td><td>13 months at most (390 days)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>_ga_{GA4_ID.replace('G-', '')}</code></td><td>Google Analytics</td><td>Keep the state of the current visit</td><td>13 months at most (390 days)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">These lifetimes are not extended on each visit; Google’s default is 2 years and the site shortens it.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text mt-8 mb-4">Audience measurement with Google Analytics</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        The site uses Google Analytics 4 to count visits and see which pages are useful: pages viewed, referring
        page, visit length, device and browser type, approximate country and city. The IP address is anonymised:
        Google Analytics 4 neither logs nor stores it. The page address sent to Google is stripped of its
        parameters, so your balances and rates are never included. Ad storage, ad user data, ad personalization and
        Google signals are switched off, and measurement data is shared with no advertiser.
      </p>
      <ul class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        <li><strong>Who processes it</strong>: Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland, acting on the publisher’s behalf (Article 28 GDPR). Data may be transferred to Google LLC in the United States under the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework and the European Commission’s standard contractual clauses.</li>
        <li><strong>Purpose</strong>: audience measurement.</li>
        <li><strong>Retention</strong>: 14 months for visit-level and identifier-level data, then deletion; only anonymous totals remain.</li>
        <li><strong>Basis</strong>: the publisher’s legitimate interests; for visitors in the European Union, Article 6(1)(f) of the GDPR. No personal information is sold or shared within the meaning of the CCPA/CPRA.</li>
        <li><strong>Opting out</strong>: block or delete cookies in your browser settings, or install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>. The calculators work exactly the same.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text mt-8 mb-4">Anonymous stability monitoring</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        To catch script errors, slow page loads, buttons that do nothing when clicked or scrolling problems, the
        site runs <strong>Microsoft Clarity in cookieless mode</strong>. In that mode Clarity sets none of
        <code>_clck</code>, <code>_clsk</code>, <code>MUID</code> or <code>CLID</code>. Every page view gets its own
        identifier, so page views and visits are never linked into a profile. Page text and everything typed into
        a field are masked in your browser before anything is sent: Microsoft never sees a balance or an APR.
      </p>
      <ul class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        <li><strong>Who processes it</strong>: Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited, One Microsoft Place, South County Business Park, Leopardstown, Dublin 18, Ireland, with possible processing in the United States; see <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Microsoft’s privacy statement</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Purpose</strong>: a technical, anonymous check that the payoff calculators load and return results.</li>
        <li><strong>Retention</strong>: 30 days for page-view recordings, 13 months for aggregated statistics.</li>
        <li><strong>Basis</strong>: the publisher’s legitimate interest in calculators that work; for visitors in the European Union, Article 6(1)(f) of the GDPR.</li>
        <li><strong>Opting out</strong>: block <code>clarity.ms</code> in your browser or content blocker (the calculators work exactly the same), or email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text mt-8 mb-4">Hosting logs</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        The site is served by GitHub Pages (GitHub, Inc.), whose servers log technical details of each request
        (IP address, time, page requested, browser) for security and reliability. The publisher has no access to
        those logs and does not use them.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text mt-8 mb-4">If you email us</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        A message to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> is used only to answer you. Your
        address is not put on a mailing list, sold or shared.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text mt-8 mb-4">Children's privacy</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        The site is not directed to children under 13 and does not knowingly collect information from children.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text mt-8 mb-4">Your rights</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        We do not sell or share personal information within the meaning of the California Consumer Privacy Act or
        other US state privacy laws, and we usually hold no data that identifies you, apart from emails you send us.
        Visitors from the European Union also have the GDPR rights of access, rectification, erasure and objection,
        and may complain to the {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority}. For audience measurement and stability monitoring you can also contact Google or Microsoft.
        Concerns about unfair practices can be reported to the US Federal Trade Commission at
        <a href="https://reportfraud.ftc.gov/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">reportfraud.ftc.gov</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text mt-8 mb-4">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        If the way the site works changes, this page is updated first and the date at the top moves forward. See
        also the <a href="/legal/">legal notice and disclaimer</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <OfficialSources />
</Layout>
